"use strict";(self.webpackChunkhalt_website=self.webpackChunkhalt_website||[]).push([["55240"],{74238(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"tag":{"label":"Rats","permalink":"/docs/tags/rats","allTagsPath":"/docs/tags","count":31,"items":[{"id":"Rats/getting-started/rat-care-guide","title":"A Comprehensive Guide to Rat Care","description":"Rats are intelligent, social, and engaging pets that bring a unique joy to any home. To ensure they live long, happy, and healthy lives, it\u2019s essential to understand and meet their specific needs. This guide provides a comprehensive overview of daily and weekly care routines for your pet rats.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/getting-started/rat-care-guide"},{"id":"general-care/health-and-medical/skin-issues","title":"A Guide to Common Skin Issues in Small Pets","description":"A comprehensive guide to identifying, preventing, and treating common skin problems in small exotic pets, including urine scald, mites, ringworm, and bacterial infections, with species-specific advice.","permalink":"/docs/general-care/health-and-medical/skin-issues"},{"id":"Rats/breeds-and-genetics/rat-variety-guide","title":"A Guide to Fancy Rat Varieties","description":"Welcome to the colorful world of fancy rats! Through selective breeding, pet rats have been developed in a stunning array of colors, coat types, and markings. While these varieties are fascinating,...","permalink":"/docs/Rats/breeds-and-genetics/rat-variety-guide"},{"id":"Rats/getting-started/rat-nutrition-guide","title":"A Guide to Proper Rat Nutrition","description":"Proper nutrition is the cornerstone of your pet rat\'s health and longevity. As omnivores, rats have specific dietary needs that must be met to prevent obesity, nutritional deficiencies, and other...","permalink":"/docs/Rats/getting-started/rat-nutrition-guide"},{"id":"Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/rat-respiratory-infections-uris-guide","title":"A Guide to Respiratory Infections (URIs) in Rats","description":"Respiratory illness is one of the most common health issues affecting pet rats. Nearly all domestic rats are carriers of Mycoplasma pulmonis, the primary bacterium responsible for these infections...","permalink":"/docs/Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/rat-respiratory-infections-uris-guide"},{"id":"Rats/health-and-wellness/rat-introductions","title":"A Guide to Safe and Successful Rat Introductions","description":"Introducing a new rat to your existing group (or \'mischief\') is an exciting step, but it must be handled with care and patience. Rats are territorial and have complex social hierarchies. A proper...","permalink":"/docs/Rats/health-and-wellness/rat-introductions"},{"id":"Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/common-health-issues","title":"Common Health Issues in Rats","description":"An overview of the most common health issues affecting pet rats, focusing on the chronic nature of Mycoplasma respiratory infections, the high incidence of mammary tumors, and conditions like bumblefoot.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/common-health-issues"},{"id":"Rats/getting-started/the-ideal-rat-habitat-guide","title":"Creating the Ideal Habitat for Your Pet Rats","description":"A well-designed habitat is crucial for the health, happiness, and safety of your pet rats. As active, intelligent, and social creatures, they need a space that supports their natural behaviors like...","permalink":"/docs/Rats/getting-started/the-ideal-rat-habitat-guide"},{"id":"Rats/health-and-wellness/dental-health","title":"Dental Health in Rats","description":"A guide to dental health in rats, focusing on the causes and prevention of incisor overgrowth (malocclusion) and the importance of providing a proper diet and chew toys.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/health-and-wellness/dental-health"},{"id":"Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/diabetes-in-rats","title":"Diabetes in Rats","description":"Diabetes Mellitus is a condition in which the body either fails to produce enough insulin or cannot use it effectively, resulting in persistently high blood sugar (hyperglycemia). While not common in pet rats, it does occur \u2014 particularly in older or overweight individuals \u2014 and requires prompt veterinary attention and a committed management plan. Understanding the signs, how diagnosis works, and what treatment looks like can make a significant difference for an affected rat 1.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/diabetes-in-rats"},{"id":"general-care/health-and-medical/entropion","title":"Entropion in Small Pets","description":"A comprehensive guide to entropion \u2014 the inward rolling of the eyelid \u2014 in small pets including rabbits, hamsters, guinea pigs, and rats. Covers causes, clinical signs, diagnosis, and treatment options.","permalink":"/docs/general-care/health-and-medical/entropion"},{"id":"Rats/getting-started/essential-rat-supplies","title":"Essential Rat Supplies","description":"Bringing pet rats home requires some preparation. Rats are intelligent, social animals with specific needs, and having the right supplies in place before they arrive will make the transition much smoother for both you and your new companions. This guide covers everything you need to set up a safe, comfortable, and enriching home for your rats.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/getting-started/essential-rat-supplies"},{"id":"Rats/health-and-wellness/eye-and-vision-issues","title":"Eye & Vision Issues in Rats","description":"A guide to common eye and vision issues in rats, explaining the significance of porphyrin (red tears) as a health indicator and discussing common infections and age-related blindness.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/health-and-wellness/eye-and-vision-issues"},{"id":"Rats/health-and-wellness/gi-health","title":"Gastrointestinal (GI) Health in Rats","description":"A guide to gastrointestinal (GI) health in rats, covering their omnivorous digestive system and the common causes of diarrhea, including diet, stress, and secondary effects from other illnesses.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/health-and-wellness/gi-health"},{"id":"Rats/getting-started/grooming-your-rat","title":"Grooming Your Rat","description":"Learn the best practices for rat grooming, including when and how to bathe them, how to trim their nails, and how to encourage their natural self-grooming habits.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/getting-started/grooming-your-rat"},{"id":"Rats/health-and-wellness/home-health-care","title":"Home Health Care for Rats","description":"Learn how to perform a routine at-home health check for your pet rats to catch early signs of illness and ensure their long-term well-being.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/health-and-wellness/home-health-care"},{"id":"Rats/getting-started/is-a-rat-right-for-me","title":"Is a Rat Right for Me and My Family?","description":"Rats are among the most intelligent, affectionate, and interactive small pets you can keep. They learn their names, come when called, enjoy being held and carried, and form genuine bonds with their...","permalink":"/docs/Rats/getting-started/is-a-rat-right-for-me"},{"id":"Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/kidney-and-urinary-disorders","title":"Kidney and Urinary Disorders in Rats","description":"An in-depth guide to kidney and urinary disorders in rats, with a focus on Chronic Progressive Nephropathy (CPN), a common age-related disease.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/kidney-and-urinary-disorders"},{"id":"Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/leptospirosis","title":"Leptospirosis in Rats","description":"An important guide to leptospirosis in rats, a zoonotic bacterial disease, explaining its transmission, signs, and the critical importance of hygiene for pet owners.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/leptospirosis"},{"id":"Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/mycoplasma-in-rats","title":"Mycoplasma in Rats: An Essential Guide","description":"If you\'re a rat owner, you\'ve likely heard the term \'myco.\' Mycoplasma pulmonis is a species of bacteria that is the primary cause of chronic respiratory disease (CRD) in pet rats. It\'s a pervasive...","permalink":"/docs/Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/mycoplasma-in-rats"},{"id":"Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/parasites-in-rats","title":"Parasites in Pet Rats","description":"Parasites are a relatively common health concern in pet rats and can affect even well-cared-for animals. Most infestations are highly treatable when caught early. This guide explains the types of parasites rats can carry, how to recognize them, how to treat them safely, and how to prevent future infestations.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/parasites-in-rats"},{"id":"Rats/health-and-wellness/parasites","title":"Parasites in Rats","description":"A guide to common parasites affecting pet rats, including the intense itching caused by fur mites and lice, and the importance of veterinary-prescribed treatment.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/health-and-wellness/parasites"},{"id":"Rats/care-and-husbandry/playing-and-training","title":"Playing with and Training Your Rat","description":"A guide to playing with and training your pet rats, offering ideas for enrichment, toys, and teaching simple tricks to engage their intelligence.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/care-and-husbandry/playing-and-training"},{"id":"Rats/getting-started/proper-handling","title":"Proper Handling of Pet Rats","description":"Learn the best techniques for safely and confidently handling your pet rats, building a strong bond based on trust and positive reinforcement.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/getting-started/proper-handling"},{"id":"Rats/health-and-wellness/rat-dental-care","title":"Rat Dental Care Guide","description":"Dental health is one of the most important \u2014 and most overlooked \u2014 aspects of rat care. Because rat incisors grow continuously throughout life, they must wear down properly to prevent serious complications. A rat with dental problems will struggle to eat, lose weight rapidly, and can deteriorate quickly. Understanding how rat teeth work and how to support healthy dental wear is essential for every rat owner.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/health-and-wellness/rat-dental-care"},{"id":"Rats/breeds-and-genetics/rat-sexing-guide","title":"Rat Sexing Guide: How to Identify Male and Female Rats at Different Ages","description":"Correctly sexing rats is essential to prevent accidental litters and ensure proper housing. Rats can reproduce very young, and misidentification is one of the most common causes of surprise...","permalink":"/docs/Rats/breeds-and-genetics/rat-sexing-guide"},{"id":"Rats/getting-started/rat-treat-guide","title":"Rat Treat Guide","description":"This guide is meant to help you quickly check whether a food is generally safe as a treat for your rats. Research on rat nutrition is limited, so some guidance is based on related species or...","permalink":"/docs/Rats/getting-started/rat-treat-guide"},{"id":"Rats/health-and-wellness/respiratory-issues","title":"Respiratory Issues in Rats (Mycoplasmosis)","description":"An in-depth guide to chronic respiratory disease in pet rats, caused by Mycoplasma pulmonis, covering the signs, triggers, and lifelong management of this ubiquitous condition.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/health-and-wellness/respiratory-issues"},{"id":"Rats/health-and-wellness/understanding-rat-behavior","title":"Understanding Rat Behavior: A Guide for Owners","description":"Rats are intelligent, social, and emotionally complex animals. Understanding their natural behaviors and unique ways of communicating is key to building a strong bond and providing them with the best...","permalink":"/docs/Rats/health-and-wellness/understanding-rat-behavior"},{"id":"Rats/care-and-husbandry/hairless-rats","title":"What to Know About Hairless Rats","description":"A guide to caring for hairless rats, explaining their genetic background, unique care needs regarding temperature, diet, and skin health, and common health issues.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/care-and-husbandry/hairless-rats"},{"id":"Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/worms","title":"Worms in Pet Rats","description":"A guide to common internal worms in pet rats, such as pinworms and tapeworms, explaining that they are often asymptomatic and how they are diagnosed and treated.","permalink":"/docs/Rats/illnesses-and-conditions/worms"}],"unlisted":false}}')}}]);